# Working data. The Export button writes two files per run.
#
# redteam-lab-full-*.json  = EVERY row, including competition_restricted and
#                            employer_confidential. Never commit this.
# redteam-lab-*.jsonl      = filtered by disclosure class at export time.
#                            The default export is public rows only, which is the
#                            file that can safely become a published dataset.
#
# Default posture is to ignore both. When you deliberately want to publish a
# public-only export, force-add that one file:
#     git add -f logs/redteam-lab-2026-08-06.jsonl

logs/

# resources/ holds third-party OWASP PDFs (their copyright, not ours to
# redistribute) and an internal synthesis brief that maps them to a private
# engagement. Kept local, never published.
resources/

# Personal Obsidian vault config, not part of the tool.
.obsidian/

# Never, under any circumstances
*full*.json
.env
*.key

# --- Added 2026-08-20 (audit remediation, item 1/4). ---------------------------
# The ledger BINARY + its rebuild source stay local: attempts.db holds the raw
# `payload` column and the owai-master internal-target rows. The PUBLISHED artifact
# is the payload-free learn/attempts-snapshot.md (written by `attempts.py export`,
# internal rows withheld by default). Never commit the DB, its backups, or the seeds.
attempts.db
attempts.db.bak-*
*.db
seed-*.json

# Scratch + the local audit report (references sensitive filenames).
tmp/
AUDIT-*.md

# Live attacker scripts and raw-payload banks. Reference by ID in chat, never publish
# (G-SATURATION). These are the files the audit flagged as the real public-exposure risk.
solace-attack.py
learn/harvest/*payload*
learn/harvest/*arsenal*
learn/harvest/*idea-bank*
learn/harvest/*ready-payloads.md
learn/harvest/*-netdeck.md
learn/harvest/*netdeck-dump*
learn/harvest/*attacks-raw*
learn/harvest/*seam-levers*
learn/harvest/grayswan-ipi-aug26-log.md
learn/harvest/agentbreaker-apps-log.md
# To publish a specific payload-free harvest file deliberately, force-add it:
#     git add -f learn/harvest/grayswan-luckybreak-defense-playbook.md

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
